/* =====================================================================
   TYPICAL CAUSES OF SLOW QUERIES ON LARGE TABLES

   SYMPTOM                        LIKELY CAUSE               FIX
   ------------------------------ -------------------------- ------------------------------------
   High logical reads             Table / index scan         Add proper index, rewrite filter
   SELECT * on wide tables        Excess I/O                 Select only the needed columns
   Function on column in WHERE    Non-SARGable predicate     Use a range:
     (e.g. YEAR(col) = 2025)                                    col >= '2025-01-01'
                                                                AND col < '2026-01-01'
   Implicit conversion            varchar vs nvarchar        Match the data types
   Bad plan after param change    Parameter sniffing         OPTION (RECOMPILE) or Query Store
                                                              forced plan
   Big DELETE / UPDATE            Log growth, lock           Batch in chunks of 5k-10k rows
                                  escalation
   PAGEIOLATCH_SH waits           Disk I/O pressure          Better indexes, more memory
   LCK_M_* waits                  Blocking                   Shorten transactions, consider RCSI
   ===================================================================== */


